# GrowPulse environment variables — COPY THIS FILE TO `.env` AND FILL IN.
# `.env` is gitignored. NEVER commit real keys. Only this example goes to git.
#
# Local CLI/Streamlit:  create .env next to app.py
# Streamlit Cloud:      App settings -> Secrets -> paste the same KEY=VALUE lines

# --- Groq (optional AI drafting; the deterministic writers work without it) -------
# Paste your key in .env (local) or Streamlit Secrets (cloud) — NEVER here in git.
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# --- MCP file targets (optional overrides; defaults shown) ------------------------
# GROWW_NOTES_PATH=product_pulse/product_notes.md
# GROWW_DRAFTS_DIR=output/drafts
# GROWW_AUDIT_LOG=output/mcp_audit_log.jsonl

# --- Real email integration (NOT configured by default) ---------------------------
# GrowPulse creates LOCAL email drafts only (.eml with X-Unsent:1) and cannot send.
# To wire a real mail tool through MCP later, provide one of:
#   GMAIL_MCP_COMMAND=   (command to launch a Gmail MCP server, e.g. npx @gmail/mcp-server)
#   ZAPIER_MCP_TOKEN=    (Zapier MCP connector token)
#   MAKE_WEBHOOK_URL=    (Make.com scenario webhook that creates the draft)
# Then add an approval-gated tool in src/mcp_server.py that calls it. Nothing
# sends without passing the same approval gate.
